1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Now the Jenkins web interface, version two point five eight, open on localhost port eight thousand ninety, already logged in as admin.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,000
This is the dashboard.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,000
It lists the jobs.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,000
We have one, called hotel booking, which is the continuous integration job for our project.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:27,000
The little weather icon and the last success and last failure columns summarise its health.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:29,000
The job page.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,000
On the left is the build history, the newest first.

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:39,000
In the middle, the stage view draws every build as a row and every pipeline stage as a column.

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Green is success.

10
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,000
The red cells in build number two and nine are the deliberate failures.

11
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,000
The test result trend shows the number of passed tests growing as the project grew.

12
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The job configuration, opened read only.

13
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,000
I will not save anything.

14
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:03,000
First: this project is parameterized, with APP ENV, BRANCH and REGISTRY.

15
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Then build triggers: Poll SCM, every five minutes, which makes Jenkins check Git for new commits.

16
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,000
This is the continuous integration trigger.

17
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Then the pipeline: the definition is Pipeline script from SCM, the repository URL, the branch specifier, which uses the BRANCH parameter, and the script path, Jenkinsfile.

18
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Now one real build, number eleven, from the twentieth of October.

19
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:41,000
It was started with the parameters staging, branch develop and the local registry.

20
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Its name, one point one point zero, dash one c two one zero three c, is the version and the commit.

21
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:56,000
The page shows the status, the duration, and the links to the console output, the test result, and the artifacts.

22
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:01,000
The console output is the complete log.

23
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,000
First the commit being built.

24
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Then the dependencies are installed with pip, from the pinned requirements.

25
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Then flake8, the linter, runs and finds nothing, so it prints nothing.

26
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Then eighty five unit and integration tests pass.

27
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Then five Selenium tests pass, and the rest are deselected.

28
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
The log ends with finished, success.

29
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Jenkins also reads the JUnit XML reports and shows them as a test result page.

30
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Here are the two test suites, with the number of tests, failures and the duration of each.

31
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Because the reports are published after every build, Jenkins can draw the trend we saw before, and a failing test appears here by name.

32
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Every build archives its artifacts.

33
00:02:51,000 --> 00:03:00,000
In the dist folder: the source archive, a tar gz file named with the version and commit, and its sha two five six checksum.

34
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:07,000
In the reports folder: the test reports, the health check answer and the deployment record.

35
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:12,000
They are kept with the build, so any build can be reproduced or checked later.

36
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Back on the job page: the build history and the trend.

37
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Jenkins keeps the last twenty builds.

38
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:27,000
Over the project, the number of passing tests grew, and the failures are the two deliberate experiments.

39
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:35,000
This is continuous integration at work: every change is built and tested, and the result is visible to everyone.


